# poe2trade.utils Submodule

## Overview

The `poe2trade.utils` package contains the shared helpers used by the offline
data pipeline and the StashSage desktop overlays. It covers chart generation,
clipboard/item parsing, feature engineering, model inference, scraping helpers,
icon generation, and release artifact utilities.

Use the Python versions supported by the root package: Python 3.11, 3.12, or
3.13. Python 3.14 is not supported yet because some pinned native wheels are
not published for it.

## Key Modules

1) `chart_utils.py`
   - Renders overlay charts and tables for supervised predictions.
   - Generates bucket-confidence and distribution-profile visuals.
   - Used by `poe2trade/app/gui_tk.py`.

2) `gui_utils.py`
   - Parses copied item text, normalizes quality/defence values, flattens
     rolled mod patterns, and builds feature DataFrames.
   - Exposes `main(text, key)` and prepared-call helpers used by the overlays.
   - Defines defence-pattern constants used to hide raw AR/EV/ES modifiers in
     the UI while keeping normalized defence features.

3) `log_utils.py`
   - Reverse-scans and parses Path of Exile client logs into trade rows.
   - Deduplicates offers by buyer, item name, amount, and currency.

4) `matrix_utils.py`
   - Builds overlay and model feature matrices from parsed parquet files.
   - Handles armour defence normalization, jewellery quality deflation, and
     belt charm-slot feature collapse.
   - Used by `poe2trade/db/matrix_cat.py`.

5) `ml_super_utils.py`
   - Loads supervised regressors, aligns runtime features to trained models,
     predicts prices, aggregates model outputs, and applies bucket statistics.
   - Used by the supervised overlay and scoring pipeline.

6) `ml_unsuper_utils.py`
   - Loads KNN bundles and returns nearest-neighbor comparisons after applying
     the runtime price filter.
   - Used by the Price Mirror overlay.

7) `parse_utils.py`
   - Flattens trade API JSON and copied item text into normalized item fields,
     mod patterns, prices, quality, and defences.
   - Shared by parsing, matrix generation, and runtime clipboard handling.

8) `score_super_utils.py`
   - Scores feature matrices with trained supervised models.
   - Writes scoring sidecars and `category_segment_stats.json`, including the
     distribution profiles consumed by the runtime overlay.

9) `train_utils.py`
   - Trains supervised and unsupervised model artifacts.
   - Writes model readmes and feature-importance manifests when available.

10) Legacy scraper helpers
   - Browser-driven and direct-request scraping helpers live under
     `poe2trade/db/legacy_scrapers/`.
   - Used by the offline data acquisition flow.

11) `get_icon_utils.py`
   - Rebuilds `db/files/base_images.json` and downloads base-type icons into
     `db/base_icons/`.

12) `super_artifact_utils.py`
   - Promotes generated supervised scoring sidecars into `db/super_models/` so
     release validation and downstream sync use the same artifacts that runtime
     code will load.

## Data Flow

1. Scrape JSON into `poe2trade/db/files/<Category>/`.
2. Parse JSON into aggregated tables.
3. Build overlay and model matrices.
4. Train supervised and unsupervised models.
5. Score supervised models and promote scoring sidecars.
6. The app loads generated per-user assets first, falling back to bundled
   package assets when no generated copy exists.

